I haven't opened your code, so this is based on the symptom, which points to missing or index-based keys.

**Cause:** Flutter matches each tile's `State` to a list position unless the items have stable keys. The expanded flag lives in that `State`. When you delete the expanded item, the next item slides into its slot and picks up the old `State`, so it appears open.

**Fix:** Key the outermost widget your item builder returns by a stable item id, not by index, title, or a random value.

```dart
ReorderableListView.builder(
  itemCount: todos.length,
  onReorder: onReorder,
  itemBuilder: (context, index) {
    final todo = todos[index];
    return TodoTile(
      key: ValueKey(todo.id), // stable id, on the outermost widget
      todo: todo,
      onDelete: () => onDelete(todo.id),
    );
  },
)
```

Things to check in your code:
- **Key placement:** if the tile is wrapped, for example in a `Dismissible`, `Padding`, or drag-listener widget, the key must be on the outermost widget. A key on an inner `ExpansionTile` won't help.
- **Key source:** `ValueKey(index)` and `ValueKey(todo.title)` reproduce the bug, the latter whenever titles repeat. If items have no id, add one when they are created.
- **State location:** keep the expanded flag local to the tile, as you have it. Stable keys fix this without moving state into the list. Hoist it only if something else, like an "expand all" button, needs to control it.

**Regression test** (adjust finders to your widgets):

```dart
testWidgets('deleting an expanded item does not expand the next one', (tester) async {
  await tester.pumpWidget(testApp(todos: [a, b, c]));

  await tester.tap(find.text(a.title));      // expand A
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();
  await tester.tap(find.byKey(Key('delete-${a.id}')));
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();

  expect(find.text(b.title), findsOneWidget);
  expect(find.text(b.details), findsNothing); // B stays collapsed
});

testWidgets('expanded state follows the item after a sibling is deleted', (tester) async {
  await tester.pumpWidget(testApp(todos: [a, b, c]));

  await tester.tap(find.text(b.title));      // expand B
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();
  await tester.tap(find.byKey(Key('delete-${a.id}')));
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();

  expect(find.text(b.details), findsOneWidget); // B is still expanded
});
```

